From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:04:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sqllab): keep editor changes made while the tab state is
 being saved

EditorAutoSync marked the editors it had just saved with the time the
PUT /tabstateview/<id> response arrived. A change typed while that request
was in flight is older than the response, so it was taken as already saved:
the next debounce found nothing unsaved, the change was never sent, and a
reload showed the previous SQL. Take the timestamp before sending, so only
what the request carried counts as saved.

